{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1TI",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let as many servants as are under the yoke count their own masters worthy of all honor, that the name of God and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doctrine may not be blasphemed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they that have believing masters, let them not despise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", because they are brethren; but rather do ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " service, because they are faithful and beloved, partakers of the benefit. These things teach and exhort.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man teacheth otherwise, and consenteth not to wholesome words, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and the doctrine which is according to godliness,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is proud, knowing nothing, but doting about questions and strifes of words, from which cometh envy, strife, railings, evil surmisings,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Perverse disputings of men of corrupt minds, and destitute of the truth, supposing gain to be godliness: from such withdraw thyself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But godliness with contentment is great gain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we brought nothing into ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " world, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " certain we can carry nothing out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And having food and raiment, with these let us be content.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But they that will be rich, fall into temptation, and a snare, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "into",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many foolish and hurtful lusts, which drown men in destruction and perdition.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the love of money is the root of all evil: which while some have coveted, they have erred from the faith, and pierced themselves through with many sorrows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou, O man of God, flee from these things; and follow after righteousness, godliness, faith, love, patience, meekness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fight the good fight of faith, lay hold on eternal life, to which thou art also called, and hast professed a good profession before many witnesses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I give thee charge in the sight of God, who maketh alive all things, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "before",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Christ Jesus, who before Pontius Pilate testified a good confession;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou keep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "this",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " commandment without spot, unrebukable, until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which in his times he will show ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who only hath immortality, dwelling in the light which no man can approach; whom no man hath seen, nor can see: to whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " honor and power everlasting. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Charge them that are rich in this world, that they be not high-minded, nor trust in uncertain riches, but in the living God, who giveth us richly all things to enjoy;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they do good, that they be rich in good works, ready to distribute, willing to communicate;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Laying up in store for themselves a good foundation against the time to come, that they may lay hold on eternal life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Timothy, keep that which is committed to thy trust, avoiding profane ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vain babblings, and oppositions of science falsely so called;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TI.6.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1TI.6.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which some professing, have erred concerning the faith. Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
